Stringent Allow Lists: We have adopted strict allow lists that define which code constructs are permissible, effectively reducing the likelihood of code injection. Only explicitly approved inputs and operations are permitted in critical execution paths.
	•	Input Validation on Dynamic Code Execution: For any dynamically constructed code that invokes a function, we perform rigorous validation checks beyond simple alphanumeric verification. This helps ensure that only safe and intended operations are carried out, mitigating risks associated with malicious input.
	•	Avoidance of User Input in File System Operations: In operations involving the file system, we design workflows to avoid the use of direct user input wherever possible. This minimizes the attack surface and helps prevent unauthorized access or manipulation of file resources.